  "hints": [
    "Values strictly below n mean integers in range(n), NOT including n itself.",
    "For small n, loop and add numbers where i % 3 == 0 or i % 5 == 0. For huge n, use arithmetic progression sum_k(m) = k * m * (m + 1) // 2 and apply inclusion-exclusion: sum(3) + sum(5) - sum(15).",
    "Pseudocode:\n  if n <= 0: return 0\n  limit = n - 1\n  def arith(step):\n      count = limit // step\n      return step * count * (count + 1) // 2\n  return arith(3) + arith(5) - arith(15)"
  ],
